line 8 extra: by-design spec §1.2 arrays are homogeneous, so an array literal's elements must share one type
line 8 type: by-design spec §1.2 arrays are homogeneous, so an array literal's elements must share one type
line 10 type: bug SUB-1196 (literal under an expected type) a literal checked against an expected type takes that type, where tsc keeps its own
line 11 type: by-design spec §Excluded-Features there is no `any`, so an unannotated `let x = []` is `never[]`, where tsc makes it an evolving `any[]`
